WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.010
Speaker 1: All right, let's get into audience
questions for the week, very important political

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.019
issues and many other things to talk about.

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:11.070
Really important issue right off the top relates
to foreign policy.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.570
I got a bunch of questions that were basically
some version of this.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:21.020
Why do Trump supporters suddenly not want
us to leave Afghanistan, which Joe Biden is

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:25.700
doing, given that it was Donald Trump's idea?

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.480
Do you really don't know the answer to this
one?

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.320
I mean, listen, guys, that they liked it when
it was Trump's idea, but not when it's Joe

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.109
Biden doing it.

00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:36.030
Look at the Iraq war.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:44.059
George W. Bush in 2003 says it doesn't actually
say, but says even though it was not Iraq

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:48.710
that attacked us on 9/11, George W. Bush says
we're going to go into Iraq.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:55.120
And whether it was trying to finish what his
father, George H.W. Bush, left undone or a

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:01.239
cynical political ploy because Saddam Hussein
was widely seen and accurately so is not a

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:06.490
particularly good guy, whatever the reason
was at that time, if you questioned what the

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.610
hell are we doing in Iraq?

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.880
You were called unpatriotic.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.740
You were accused of not supporting the troops,
et cetera, incomes Trump and Trump says, hey,

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.740
you know what?

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.560
I was against going into Iraq.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.720
That was a disaster.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.750
I'm going to fix the Republican Party.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.300
I'm not going to do stupid stuff like George
W. Bush.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:29.940
And by and large, his followers in twenty,
fifteen, twenty sixteen fell for that, which

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.140
13 years before would have been unthinkable
in most Republican circles, except for some

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.530
like more extreme traditional libertarian
circles.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.150
That's what Democrats have been saying all
along.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.700
But when Trump says it, they believe it.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.380
And it's the exact same thing with Afghanistan,
Trump said.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.480
We're getting the hell out of Afghanistan.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.970
And I'll talk about whether that makes sense
in a moment.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.050
Hint it does.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:59.500
And then when Joe Biden came in to office
and at the time, Republicans sort of said

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.500
they liked it.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.979
I mean, I guess Joe Biden came in and said,
listen, I'm not saying we're not getting out

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:06.460
of Afghanistan, but Trump is such a buffoon.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.840
My words, not his.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.549
I'm pausing everything Trump was doing to
review it.

00:02:11.549 --> 00:02:13.189
And then I'll make a decision.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:18.239
And Joe Biden made the decision he's going
to keep going with the Afghanistan withdrawal.

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:20.040
And it will.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.709
The announcement was instead of being in May,
which was Trump's idea, it will be by September

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:29.420
11th, a delay of about four months, even though
it appears to be happening more quickly and

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:34.010
will be done roughly similarly to when Donald
Trump says it's basically the same thing that

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:35.859
Joe Biden is doing is what Donald Trump is
doing.

00:02:35.859 --> 00:02:40.620
But now all these Republicans and Trump are
saying, whoa, hold on a second, Joe Biden

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.329
has no plan for how to get out.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.749
Did Trump he just said, we're leaving.

00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:49.389
Joe Biden is getting out in a way that could
leave a vacuum.

00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:51.040
That's always been the concern.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.360
What's new about that?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.680
So they're just pathetic political statements.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.980
I wouldn't pay too much attention to them.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:04.160
For the most part, foreign policy in this
way, I don't believe is really even going

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.390
to play a role in twenty twenty four unless
something dramatically changes.

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:15.329
So it's very transparent cynicism and the
analysis is super simple.

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:18.739
They liked it when Trump was doing it, when
Biden's doing it.

00:03:18.739 --> 00:03:23.879
By definition, it's not good because Biden,
as they see it, is incompetent and won't do

00:03:23.879 --> 00:03:27.859
it the right way now in terms of getting out.

00:03:27.859 --> 00:03:33.290
It's just time, and I've said for a long time,
when you break something, you own it, then

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.430
you've got to fix it.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:40.180
And so when this applied to Afghanistan in
this applied to Iraq, when you go in, as the

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:46.180
United States did, and wreak havoc and cause
chaos without even evaluating whether your

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.819
motivations were good or bad, like I'm not
even including that in this conversation.

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:55.310
As relevant as it is, if you caused the chaos,
you have some responsibility to fix it.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:04:01.140
And the question then becomes how many years,
how many administrations worth?

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:06.579
And at a certain point, particularly when
you realize just staying won't fix it.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.909
You have to say this is as far as the responsibility
goes and it's time to get out.

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:15.079
So are we responsible for the state of affairs
currently in Afghanistan as well as in Iraq?

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:16.850
Of course.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:22.920
Would our responsibility dictate that we stay
even if we only continue to make it worse

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.100
or at least not better?

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.810
I think there is a limit to it, and I think
that limit has been reached 20 years.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.220
So it is time to get out.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:35.450
Things may go downhill as a result, and that
is going to have to be dealt with.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.920
But at a certain point, the responsibility
has to stop.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.190
So the Trump supporters now saying Biden shouldn't
get out, but Trump was and I like that then,

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.200
but I don't like it now.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.440
Don't pay attention to them.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:50.470
But there are real serious questions about
the limits of American responsibility when

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:53.520
we get into these quagmires abroad.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:06:29.650
And that's a much bigger topic for a different
day.

